## Goal
Show how the six project samples cluster by gene expression using PCA of the gene-level counts, with points coloured by condition (untreated or treated).

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| `counts_gene` | `02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper` | `run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv` |
| `design` | `01_samplesheets` | `01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv` |

## Method
1. In the `gars-bio` environment, read the resolved gene-count TSV and the design CSV. Match samples by `sample_id`; require exactly the six design samples and their `condition` values.
2. Transform each gene count as `log2(count + 1)`, then center each gene across the six samples without scaling genes by variance. Run PCA on the sample-by-gene matrix with scikit-learn `PCA(n_components=2)`.
3. Write a PC1/PC2 scatter plot as a PNG in `results/`, with each sample labelled by `sample_id`, point colour mapped to `condition`, and axis labels showing explained variance. Save the sample coordinates and condition as a CSV. Inputs remain read-only.

## Outputs
Types come from the closed vocabulary in _references/artifact_types.md.

